  "uT": 1,
  "summary": "The on-site hippocampus session of Murphy's retired Paranormal Shakti, offered to investigators for 'intuitive perceptions' at a site: the hippocampal signal alternating between the two stereo channels of a 4-coil cross on each temporal lobe. The cited pages give no length or switching speed: 30 min and one switch per signal are project choices.",
  "setting": "On site during an investigation, at a time of geomagnetic quiet (vendor).",
  "schedule": "Vendor: after 6 temporal sessions, do 3 frontal ones (murphy-paranormal-shakti-frontal), but not in the 3 days before an investigation, because it says the frontal session lowers sensitivity. The vendor's general Shakti rules: at most every 72 h or once a week, never on consecutive days.",
  "notes": "The vendor says the on-site sessions 'alternate the signal between the two stereo channels' ('Sessions to Use On-Site During Investigations', archived 2013-05-09) and: 'Begin with the left channel vertical and the right channel horizontal.' ('Hippocampus Signal Information', archived 2013-06-05). This program runs 30 min and switches after each signal, with about 4 s of silence between. The pages give no length and no switching speed: both are project choices. Same parameters as murphy-shakti-60min-bilateral-hippocampus-slow at half the length. The coils form a cross on each temporal lobe (FT7, C5, TP7, T9 and FT8, C6, TP8, T10; the site names are this project's reading). One channel drives the top and bottom coils, the other the front and back coils. Each pair has one positive and one negative coil, after the 8 Coil Shakti coil chart: C5, FT7, T10 and TP8 are reversed. The hippocampal signal is the primed burst: one pulse, then four pulses 170 ms later, three times in 0.74 s (after Tsang 2004 p.5 [1017]). It is rebuilt from a description: the vendor's file is not published. The vendor's 10 to 50 mG carries no distance (measurement.htm, duds.htm); an independent meter read 0.1 to 1.0 uT RMS about 9 cm from the coils (Gendle 2012 p.11 [227]). This program's setting is the peak field 20 mm in front of each coil. The effect is a vendor claim; what you experience is not evidence about the site. Independent sham-controlled tests of God-Helmet-type fields found no field effect (Granqvist 2005, double-blind; Gendle & McGrath 2012, where the experimenter knew the condition). The vendor: 'Headaches have occured with this signal when used only over the right side of the head'. If headache or pressure appears, lower the intensity by one third. The product is retired; this program is of historical interest. Not for people with epilepsy; stop at once on fear or distress.",
